# mypki .gitignore
#
# Two rules govern everything below. (1) Runtime state never belongs in git: the CA's key material, the generated session
# secret, the issued ledger and every log line are produced by running the thing, and a commit that captures them is a leak
# with a diff attached. (2) The key-material block is deliberately broad (`*.pem`, `*.key`, `*.crt`, `*.csr`, `*.p12`) rather
# than narrowed to `<data>/ca/`, because the mistake it protects against is an operator running `mypki init-ca` in the wrong
# directory — which puts the CA key exactly here, and no amount of path-specific ignoring would notice.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
dist/
sdist/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
.eggs/
MANIFEST

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- virtualenvs
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
*.cover
.tox/
.nox/
.pre-commit-config.yaml.bak

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- editors / OS
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
*~
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- generated reports
# `reports/harness-ledger.md` and `.json` are written by tools/harness_ledger.py from a harness log, on this machine, about
# this machine's run: which ports were free, which pwsh build answered, how many scratch dirs were lying around. Committing
# them would freeze one box's numbers into the repository as if they were a property of the release, which is the exact
# confusion docs/CHANGE_POLICY.md exists to prevent. The documents link to this path instead of copying from it.
reports/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- runtime state
logs/
*.log
*.log.[0-9]*
/data/
instance/
issued.db
issued.db-*
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- key material
# Never commit any of these. `mypki-root-ca.crt` is a PUBLIC certificate and is still ignored, because the download exists
# to be fetched from the running CA rather than frozen in a repository where it silently expires.
*.pem
*.key
*.crt
*.csr
*.p12
